1
00:01:02,240 --> 00:01:03,120
My new camera.

2
00:01:03,920 --> 00:01:05,360
Try adjusting the settings.

3
00:01:05,360 --> 00:01:06,820
The lighting is good here.

4
00:01:11,640 --> 00:01:12,700
Where are we going?

5
00:01:13,800 --> 00:01:15,520
This place is quite hard to find.

6
00:01:15,520 --> 00:01:16,320
What's wrong?

7
00:01:17,039 --> 00:01:18,800
This client is a Taiwanese compatriot

8
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:19,840
named Lin Siyuan.

9
00:01:20,039 --> 00:01:20,800
His grandfather

10
00:01:20,800 --> 00:01:22,200
is from Shishan, Nan'an.

11
00:01:22,440 --> 00:01:25,160
His grandfather settled in Taiwan over 40 years ago.

12
00:01:25,160 --> 00:01:27,960
He always talks about his hometown's Shishan Powan.

13
00:01:27,960 --> 00:01:29,200
So he came back this time

14
00:01:29,200 --> 00:01:31,930
to find the taste from his grandfather's memory.

15
00:01:32,240 --> 00:01:34,400
But this shop is really hard to find.

16
00:01:34,759 --> 00:01:36,680
I've been looking for it for a long time.

17
00:01:36,680 --> 00:01:38,210
Some people online even say

18
00:01:38,520 --> 00:01:40,120
it moved away a long time ago.

19
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:43,600
It's over in the Ximei Old Town area.

20
00:01:44,920 --> 00:01:45,560
Let me see.

21
00:01:49,600 --> 00:01:51,080
Why do I keep feeling

22
00:01:52,240 --> 00:01:54,500
like someone is watching me from behind?

23
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:20,800
What's wrong?

24
00:02:21,400 --> 00:02:22,329
Where is Xinyue?

25
00:02:23,680 --> 00:02:25,560
She said she was checking out the route

26
00:02:25,560 --> 00:02:27,000
to help the client from Taiwan

27
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:28,260
find the taste of home.

28
00:02:28,440 --> 00:02:29,440
You didn't drive?

29
00:02:30,120 --> 00:02:31,650
Someone is driving for her.

30
00:02:31,760 --> 00:02:33,520
I'm happy to relax.

31
00:02:33,720 --> 00:02:35,480
Who? A newbie?

32
00:02:35,760 --> 00:02:36,840
Just a guy.

33
00:02:36,840 --> 00:02:39,440
With his styled hair and hairspray.

34
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:42,840
By the way, he said he's your landlord.

35
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:43,840
Really?

36
00:02:43,840 --> 00:02:45,760
Yeah, that whole building is his.

37
00:02:46,880 --> 00:02:48,800
What, are you jealous?

38
00:02:49,520 --> 00:02:50,850
Or do you like Li Xinyue?

39
00:03:04,680 --> 00:03:05,160
Sir.

40
00:03:06,360 --> 00:03:08,040
Do you know this place?

41
00:03:11,520 --> 00:03:12,680
I remember.

42
00:03:13,080 --> 00:03:16,040
Huang's Powan in Shishan old market.

43
00:03:17,680 --> 00:03:19,610
But due to the old town renovation,

44
00:03:19,840 --> 00:03:21,900
the businesses there all moved away.

45
00:03:23,520 --> 00:03:25,280
Do you know where they moved?

46
00:03:26,560 --> 00:03:28,560
It seems they were all relocated to

47
00:03:28,640 --> 00:03:32,000
the new market on the south bank of Xixi.

48
00:03:32,880 --> 00:03:35,400
But that was decades ago.

49
00:03:36,120 --> 00:03:37,840
Who knows where they moved to.

50
00:03:38,880 --> 00:03:39,740
Thank you, sir.

51
00:03:39,920 --> 00:03:40,560
You're welcome.

52
00:03:40,560 --> 00:03:41,280
Let's go.

53
00:03:45,079 --> 00:03:45,840
I

54
00:03:46,079 --> 00:03:47,000
like her.

55
00:03:48,680 --> 00:03:50,920
I couldn't tell you guys were so humorous.

56
00:03:50,920 --> 00:03:53,120
If you don't like him, why are you jealous?

57
00:03:53,120 --> 00:03:54,200
Jealous?

58
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:56,160
How could I be jealous?

59
00:03:56,800 --> 00:03:58,440
This is the anger of a shareholder

60
00:03:58,440 --> 00:04:00,880
who has been deprived of decision-making power.

61
00:04:00,880 --> 00:04:03,360
But we haven't even said who it is.

62
00:04:05,720 --> 00:04:07,640
I said it, okay?

63
00:04:07,800 --> 00:04:09,160
I'm talking about them.

64
00:04:09,960 --> 00:04:10,800
Okay.

65
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:12,520
When do you think they'll be back?

66
00:04:12,520 --> 00:04:14,160
What does it have to do with me?

67
00:04:14,160 --> 00:04:16,720
They can come back whenever they want.

68
00:04:17,839 --> 00:04:19,800
I just checked the weather forecast.

69
00:04:19,800 --> 00:04:22,600
It looks like it's going to rain heavily.

70
00:04:23,360 --> 00:04:25,480
It's going to rain heavily.

71
00:04:25,560 --> 00:04:27,120
Again, what does it have to do with me?

72
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:29,160
Let it rain.

73
00:04:29,960 --> 00:04:30,880
Yiyi, tell me.

74
00:04:31,120 --> 00:04:32,200
The roads are slippery in the rain.

75
00:04:32,200 --> 00:04:33,730
What if the car breaks down?

76
00:04:34,880 --> 00:04:36,520
What if the road is bad

77
00:04:36,520 --> 00:04:38,640
and the car is hard to drive?

78
00:04:39,120 --> 00:04:40,760
It's hard to drive.

79
00:04:41,040 --> 00:04:43,500
It's not like you're driving a convertible.

80
00:04:55,480 --> 00:04:58,080
I thought you took the bag out to block the rain.

81
00:04:59,520 --> 00:05:02,180
This bag is very expensive, okay, young master?

82
00:05:02,240 --> 00:05:03,920
If the bag gets ruined by the rain, you can buy a new one.

83
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:05,520
If you get sick from the rain, you'll need medicine, injections, and hospitalization.

84
00:05:05,520 --> 00:05:06,280
Look at you.

85
00:05:06,280 --> 00:05:07,400
Stop, stop, stop.

86
00:05:07,520 --> 00:05:09,360
Can't you wish me well?

87
00:05:09,680 --> 00:05:10,160
No.

88
00:05:10,280 --> 00:05:12,040
I'm not saying you're going to immediately

89
00:05:12,040 --> 00:05:13,080
need medicine, injections, and hospitalization.

90
00:05:13,080 --> 00:05:13,480
Hey,

91
00:05:13,560 --> 00:05:14,240
Li Xinyue.

92
00:05:17,440 --> 00:05:18,120
Who is it?

93
00:05:25,080 --> 00:05:26,480
A helpful citizen.

94
00:05:28,400 --> 00:05:30,730
We Nan'an people are quite enthusiastic.

95
00:05:31,640 --> 00:05:32,520
Thank you.

96
00:05:37,240 --> 00:05:38,640
Let me hold the umbrella.

97
00:05:39,480 --> 00:05:40,960
No.

98
00:05:41,320 --> 00:05:42,650
The rain is still heavy.

99
00:05:42,760 --> 00:05:43,440
Let's wait a while.

100
00:05:43,440 --> 00:05:44,560
Wait until it gets lighter.

101
00:05:44,560 --> 00:05:45,520
Just get closer to me.

102
00:05:45,520 --> 00:05:47,240
Li Xinyue, are you an idiot?

103
00:05:52,720 --> 00:05:53,800
Who is this again?

104
00:06:09,400 --> 00:06:13,040
Hardship only flows to those who can endure it.

105
00:06:20,040 --> 00:06:21,370
Zhang Yang, Zhang Yang.

106
00:06:21,800 --> 00:06:24,320
Hardship only flows to you who can endure it.

107
00:06:42,120 --> 00:06:43,680
Why are you still dawdling?

108
00:06:43,680 --> 00:06:46,010
Hurry up and come out with me to find a shop.

109
00:06:46,560 --> 00:06:47,360
What's wrong?

110
00:06:50,760 --> 00:06:51,440
Speak.

111
00:06:56,560 --> 00:06:57,840
Xinyue,

112
00:06:58,240 --> 00:07:02,440
I came back in the heavy rain yesterday and got a high fever.

113
00:07:02,600 --> 00:07:05,040
Now everything I eat is tasteless.

114
00:07:05,200 --> 00:07:09,360
My throat and head are burning with pain.

115
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:13,080
This is what Mr. Zhang wants to say to you.

116
00:07:14,080 --> 00:07:15,120
Right, Mr. Zhang?

117
00:07:18,360 --> 00:07:19,820
I can understand the rest.

118
00:07:20,200 --> 00:07:22,600
But how did you tell it's 'hot'?

119
00:07:24,480 --> 00:07:26,600
It's just a feeling.

120
00:07:28,640 --> 00:07:29,280
Come on, Zhang Yang.

121
00:07:29,280 --> 00:07:30,740
Show me the gesture again.

122
00:07:32,200 --> 00:07:33,000
Well,

123
00:07:33,720 --> 00:07:36,159
he went to pick you up in the heavy rain yesterday.

124
00:07:36,159 --> 00:07:37,640
He fell on his way back

125
00:07:37,640 --> 00:07:38,840
and scraped his knee.

126
00:07:39,040 --> 00:07:41,480
Maybe we should let him rest today.

127
00:07:44,720 --> 00:07:46,450
So you're really not faking it.

128
00:07:47,920 --> 00:07:49,520
Let me see where you're hurt.

129
00:08:10,320 --> 00:08:11,360
Alright.

130
00:08:12,600 --> 00:08:13,730
You stay home today.

131
00:08:13,760 --> 00:08:14,890
I'll go find Qin Fei.

132
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:16,720
Don't.

133
00:08:16,840 --> 00:08:19,960
Qin Fei went out to carry bags for Mr. Tang today.

134
00:08:20,800 --> 00:08:23,160
Maybe I should still go with you.

135
00:08:23,640 --> 00:08:25,720
But you have to take good care of me.

136
00:08:27,640 --> 00:08:29,240
I'll go by myself.

137
00:08:29,320 --> 00:08:30,780
You stay home and recover.

138
00:08:31,600 --> 00:08:32,440
Don't.

139
00:08:33,280 --> 00:08:35,880
Well, if I go

140
00:08:35,880 --> 00:08:38,880
with you today, can I still get my meals reimbursed?

141
00:08:39,440 --> 00:08:41,200
I can't if I stay here.

142
00:08:43,520 --> 00:08:45,200
I'll reimburse your meals.

143
00:08:45,200 --> 00:08:46,800
Remember to get the receipt.

144
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:52,530
Um, can I buy some sea cucumbers and abalones to nourish myself?

145
00:08:52,880 --> 00:08:53,480
Oh, right.

146
00:08:53,960 --> 00:08:55,440
And caviar,

147
00:08:55,520 --> 00:08:57,160
and Angus steak.

148
00:08:57,520 --> 00:09:00,920
Do you want to eat your sick meals at a Black Pearl restaurant?

149
00:09:06,360 --> 00:09:06,820
You two.

150
00:09:08,160 --> 00:09:08,840
You two.

151
00:09:10,400 --> 00:09:11,840
Singing the same tune.

152
00:09:11,840 --> 00:09:13,240
Did you rehearse this?

153
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:18,280
Okay.

154
00:09:18,800 --> 00:09:19,360
Hurry up.

155
00:09:20,040 --> 00:09:21,040
I'll take you out.

156
00:09:23,520 --> 00:09:24,880
Why are you dawdling?

157
00:09:24,880 --> 00:09:26,160
Are you waiting for me to carry you down?

158
00:09:26,160 --> 00:09:26,690
Hurry up.

159
00:09:34,440 --> 00:09:36,240
Let's take a picture here later.

160
00:09:54,800 --> 00:09:55,600
What's wrong?

161
00:10:05,400 --> 00:10:06,130
What is this?

162
00:10:12,440 --> 00:10:14,000
I know it's a ring.

163
00:10:19,640 --> 00:10:20,440
Beg me.

164
00:10:23,800 --> 00:10:25,160
Say please.

165
00:10:32,200 --> 00:10:33,930
What exactly do you want to say?

166
00:10:40,040 --> 00:10:41,840
Why is your face so red?

167
00:10:44,400 --> 00:10:45,800
You still have a fever.

168
00:10:46,440 --> 00:10:48,100
Let me take your temperature.

169
00:11:15,880 --> 00:11:18,200
You do it yourself.

170
00:11:40,200 --> 00:11:42,240
You don't have a fever.

171
00:11:50,400 --> 00:11:51,720
It's quite serious, isn't it?

172
00:11:51,720 --> 00:11:53,250
Maybe this isn't accurate.

173
00:11:53,320 --> 00:11:55,040
I'll take you to the hospital to take your rectal temperature.

174
00:11:55,040 --> 00:11:55,520
No.

175
00:12:01,320 --> 00:12:03,000
Such a loud voice.

176
00:12:03,320 --> 00:12:04,780
It doesn't seem inflamed.

177
00:12:11,800 --> 00:12:14,040
Let's drop it and get to work.

178
00:12:14,160 --> 00:12:15,440
Let's hurry up and go.
